# @tokenomik packages resolve from GitHub Packages, everything else from npmjs.
#
# The token needs only `read:packages`. Put it in your USER .npmrc
# (%USERPROFILE%\.npmrc), never in the repo:
#
#   //npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=<a PAT with read:packages>
#
# In CI, GITHUB_TOKEN already has read:packages for repos in the same org:
#
#   //npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${GITHUB_TOKEN}
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
# The package used to be installed by private git URL. That needs a git binary
# and git credentials, which no slim container base has, so `npm ci` inside an
# image build died with `npm error enoent An unknown git error occurred`. A
# registry install needs neither - just a token in .npmrc - so the tools/ci
# split that worked around it is no longer necessary.
@tokenomik:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
